cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the RSSILab Indoor Positioning Simulator in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RSSILab Indoor Positioning Simulator: GPS-free RSSI-based indoor positioning and tracking"
abstract: >-
  RSSILab Indoor Positioning Simulator (RSSILab) is a simulator for research on
  GPS-free indoor positioning and tracking based on the received signal strength. It
  builds indoor scenarios with anchors, walls and furniture, simulates the RSS of
  several radio technologies (path loss, multi-wall losses, correlated shadowing,
  fading, receiver effects), generates RSS datasets and benchmarks distance-based
  methods (trilateration, multilateration, maximum likelihood) and fingerprinting
  models trained on a simulated survey (k-NN, decision tree, random forest, neural
  network), with Monte Carlo trials and error statistics, from a GUI or from Python.
type: software
